---DOM-based---
- Review every piece of client-side javascript for sinks that may be used to access the DOM and can be controlled by client-supplied input 
- Examples sinks include:
 document.write()
 document.writeln()
 document.domain() ... etc
- Ones you identify a source that leads to a sink , supply a unique string and use developer tools to follow the path of execution to the sink
- Test candidate payloads 
- Test the attack in the browser 

